[node name="S3_Minefield" type="Node3D" parent="Sections" unique_id=61707270]
editor_description = "S3, the lava crack grid (bearings 145..200). The deck is flat at lane height; where each of the 36 demon pads stood there is now a crack in map_base.glb's own rock with lava glowing in it (hard-modelled, flush, no plate) and one of these lava_crack nodes over it: the same BoostPad trigger and footprint as the demon pad plus a heat-haze quad (maps/bentham_ring/materials/lava_haze.gdshader, one shared material). 17 rows x 3 columns (2.94 x 3.2 m); one path is cut through the grid by the cells left crack-free, three cracks left in the path (rows 1, 4, 10; trigger 2.5 x 0.5 x 2.5) have to be jumped, and the ragged rock wall at the pit edge is map_base.glb's own rock. tools/modelling/maps/bentham_ring/map_base_build.py (the S3 block) is the one layout the mesh, the collider, these node transforms and the proofs all come from; the build writes this node block. Every crack launches at the shipped 18 m/s; the 204 divider catches the flights that would leave the section. No lava hazard and no TrapVolume in this section: a launch drops you back on the same deck. SpeedPowerup is a parked leftover from the retired Split, left where it was found."

